--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Security hardening from the global code review
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Context:
The global code review found four verified security issues: Spark SQL literals
that only doubled quotes, a Databricks token captured in MLflow traces, raw HTML
in the shared toast/notification/dialog helpers, and routes without role guards.
LLM failures also surfaced the serving URL and upstream response body to users.
The user approved the security batch only; no other review item is changed.

Changes:
1. src/back/core/graph_analysis/pattern/JobPatterns.py,
   src/back/core/graph_analysis/community/JobCommunities.py,
   src/back/core/graph_analysis/community/CommunityMaterializer.py,
   src/back/core/databricks/uc/metric_sql.py
   - Hand-rolled quote-doubling replaced by SQLHelpers.sql_literal / sql_escape,
     which double backslashes for Spark (pattern_id comes from the URL path).
     CommunityMaterializer escapes per store dialect via sql_flavor().
2. src/jobs/graph_analytics_job.py, src/jobs/contract_demo.py
   - Standalone job sql_escape now doubles backslashes before quotes.
3. src/agents/agent_ontology_assistant/responses_agent.py, log_model.py,
   src/api/routers/internal/ontology.py
   - Credentials go to the agent constructor (or DATABRICKS_HOST/TOKEN when
     served), never through custom_inputs: MLflow auto-traces predict and
     predict_stream with the full request. Raw @mlflow.trace decorators that
     recorded the token argument removed; tool calls use trace_tool.
4. src/agents/llm_utils.py and 15 agent engines
   - New llm_failure_message(exc): users see the HTTP status or transport
     failure only; the full exception stays in the server log.
   - src/api/routers/internal/simulation.py recognises the new 404 summary.
5. src/front/static/global/js/utils.js, task-tracker.js and dialog callers
   - showNotification, the Notification Center, showConfirmDialog and
     showInfoDialog escape `message`. New `messageHtml` option (and
     NotificationCenter.add isHtml flag) for trusted markup; 17 callers moved
     to it with escapeHtml on every dynamic value; callers that pre-escaped
     plain text no longer double-escape.
6. src/back/core/task_manager/Task.py, TaskManager.py,
   src/api/routers/internal/tasks.py
   - Tasks record their owner from the request identity. Users see their own
     and system tasks; only the owner or an admin can cancel; clear-completed
     is admin-only.
7. src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py, home.py, src/shared/fastapi/main.py
   - /dtwin/reasoning/materialize requires domain Builder (as main.py already
     claimed). /clear-ontology requires domain Editor and is lifecycle
     status-gated. Unused /write-volume-file (unguarded write with app
     credentials) removed.
8. docs/architecture.md, docs/api.md
   - Assistant credential flow and owner-scoped task endpoints.
9. Tests
   - New: tests/units/core/test_graph_analysis_sql_escaping.py,
     tests/units/agents/test_llm_secret_hygiene.py,
     tests/units/api/test_route_authorization_hardening.py,
     tests/units/front/test_notification_escaping_contract.py.
   - Updated to the new contracts: five agent LLM-failure tests, the assistant
     invoke route test, two registry confirmation tests, and the community
     materializer test store (sql_flavor).

Follow-ups (not in this batch):
- /read-volume-file reads any path with the app credentials (needs OBO).
- agent_supervisor ResponsesAgent still reads host/token from custom_inputs
  (in-process run mode only; no caller in the app).
- Module-local raw-HTML sinks (ontology names in several renderers) remain.

